# Keep text files readable to git's own tooling, and name the real binaries.
#
# WHY: a single raw control character — a NUL, most often — makes git classify a
# file as binary, and `git diff` then prints "Binary files differ" instead of
# the change. A real edit to that file becomes invisible in review while every
# check still reports green. This was measured, not assumed: an identical file
# diffed as full text with `diff` set, and as "Binary files … differ" without.
#
# Marking a path `diff` tells git to treat it as text REGARDLESS of its content,
# which is what keeps a stray byte from hiding a whole changeset from a reviewer.
#
# SCOPE, honestly: this governs git's own tooling. `grep` and ripgrep do not
# read this file — on a NUL-bearing file they still report only
# "Binary file … matches", suppressing the line and its number, so a match
# survives but its content does not. The enforcement that covers every tool is
# `npm run check:text` (scripts/check-control-chars.mjs), which fails CI on a
# raw control byte anywhere in the tree. ESLint covers the same ground for
# .ts/.tsx only — this and the CI check extend it to Markdown, JSON, YAML, CSS.
#
# Deliberately NOT setting `text=auto` here: the repo is developed with
# core.autocrlf=true and renormalising every line ending would produce a
# whole-tree diff that buries real changes. `diff` alone changes how git READS
# a file, not how it stores it.

# ── Source and docs: always diff as text ────────────────────────────────────
*.ts        diff
*.tsx       diff
*.mjs       diff
*.js        diff
*.json      diff
*.md        diff
*.yml       diff
*.yaml      diff
*.css       diff
*.html      diff
*.txt       diff
*.py        diff
.gitignore  diff
.gitattributes diff
*.example   diff

# ── Real binaries: never diff, never normalise ──────────────────────────────
# `binary` is git's shorthand for `-diff -merge -text`. Naming them explicitly
# keeps the rules above from ever being read as applying to a font or an image.
*.woff2     binary
*.woff      binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.node      binary
